From: Uke recovery maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libmodprobe: deny automatic storage writers in recovery

The matched Uke stock recovery module list loads charger_partition, whose
probe schedules raw charger-partition writes, and ufs_ffu, which schedules
firmware-update work. Deny both before any loader path can insert them.
Force this denial in every recovery build, including when an inherited
first-stage ramdisk hides the packaged recovery executable. Keep the marker
fallback for other build variants and reject callers that disable OEM
blocklists. Preserve normal-boot behavior and the stock blocklist. Existing
dependency checks skip dependent drivers.

diff --git a/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp b/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
--- a/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
+++ b/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <sys/wait.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <map>
@@ -401,6 +402,22 @@ Modprobe::Modprobe(const std::vector<std::string>& base_paths, const std::string loa
         ParseCfg(base_path + "/modules.blocklist", blocklist_callback);
     }
 
+    // A recovery build must not depend on a packaged-executable marker:
+    // an inherited first-stage ramdisk can hide that path. Keep the marker
+    // fallback for other variants that run with the recovery ramdisk.
+    // charger_partition schedules raw partition writes on probe; ufs_ffu
+    // schedules UFS firmware-update work. Also reject their hard dependents.
+#if defined(__ANDROID_RECOVERY__)
+    const bool deny_automatic_storage_writers = true;
+#else
+    const bool deny_automatic_storage_writers = access("/system/bin/recovery", F_OK) == 0;
+#endif
+    if (deny_automatic_storage_writers) {
+        blocklist_enabled = true;
+        module_blocklist_.emplace("charger_partition");
+        module_blocklist_.emplace("ufs_ffu");
+    }
+
     ParseKernelCmdlineOptions();
 }
 
